<!--
  Keeps November.DI itself intact under managed code stripping (IL2CPP / WebGL).

  IMPORTANT: Unity reads link.xml files from Assets/ and from EMBEDDED packages (a package cloned into
  your project's Packages/ folder). It does NOT read them from packages installed through Git or a
  registry (Library/PackageCache). For those installs the package relies on [Preserve]: [Inject] and
  [Resolve] derive from PreserveAttribute, and the Func<T> / Lazy<T> helpers the container reaches by
  reflection are marked [Preserve]. To preserve the package assembly regardless of how it is installed,
  add this to a link.xml in your own Assets/ folder:

      <linker><assembly fullname="November.DI" preserve="all" /></linker>

  This file does NOT preserve YOUR types: a constructor that is only reached by reflection (a type with
  one public constructor and no [Inject]) can still be stripped. Mark the constructor [Inject], or the
  class [Preserve] (keeps its default constructor), or list the assembly in your own link.xml
  (see README, "IL2CPP and code stripping").
-->
<linker>
  <assembly fullname="November.DI" preserve="all" />
</linker>
